            "text": "In 2024, Northstar set out to increase free-to-paid conversion through its self-serve document-editing funnel. As content designer, I partnered with a product manager and a product designer to overhaul the application’s neglected catalog of in-product upgrade prompts.\n\nRather than relying on generic prompts, we mapped the copy directly to user context. We drew clear boundaries between three distinct situations: an active free allowance, an exhausted limit, and the intentional selection of a paid feature. The design rationale was deliberate: eliminate ambiguity by showing users exactly where they stood in their workflow and what the paid tier offered them at that moment.\n\nAcross the complete rollout, the upgrade-prompt program lifted paid conversion by 9% and added €200,000 in ARR. While these whole-program results belong to the combined efforts of product, design, and engineering rather than an isolated test of copy alone, they demonstrate how direct, state-aware language drives commercial momentum.",
